      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would indeed be nice.  \n\nJust want to add that as a workaround, when uploading the image, select the VRC_Cam component when you're in Build/Play mode and change the FOV from 60 to 75, then position your camera. \n\nFor some reason the cam in the editor has an FOV of 60, but the photo it takes is with 75.  I've had much better luck with photos since I found that out. :3  Hopefully it's useful to OP and others who read this.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-12-07T05:52:08.141Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So in the 2017 update we'll be able to upload a YouTube trailer for the world, so shouldn't we also be able to upload a new image for the world as well? Having to aim a camera at a quad and hoping it comes out nice is a bit archaic. It'd be a lot of nicer if we could just upload an image for the world through the site in the same way we can change the player capacity, description, tags, etc.",
